  "caption": "Uncle Quinn was minding baby Bean, who always looked left and had a slightly flat spot on the back of the head.\n\nA baby favouring one side may have a tight neck muscle, and the flat spot often follows. So care looks at the neck, not just head shape.\n\nWhat can help: starting physio early, positioning toys, talking and feeding from the less-preferred side, supervised awake tummy time several times a day, less time in capsules, bouncers and seats, and stretches taught by a physio rather than copied from videos.\n\nSee your GP or paediatrician for a sudden tilt, a squint or unusual eye movements, a neck that won't turn, a worsening shape or ridge, a neck lump, fever, vomiting or irritability.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
